{# The public front page (/): what this server is, sign-in, the API documentation, and a word for
   recipients of its mail. No session, no script; the stylesheets and font come from the application. #}
{% import 'dashboard/_icons.html.twig' as icon %}
{% import '_site.html.twig' as site %}
{% set admin = admin_email() %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    {{ site.application_meta() }}
    <meta name="description" content="A self-hosted email validation and delivery service for the client applications of this installation.">
    <title>{{ site_name() }}</title>
    {{ site.stylesheets() }}
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="topbar">
    <span class="brand">{{ icon.logo() }}<span>{{ site_name() }}</span></span>
    <a class="btn front-signin" href="{{ path('dashboard_login') }}">Sign in</a>
</header>
<main id="main" class="content">
    <div class="grid">
        <section class="front-hero g-col-4" aria-labelledby="front-h">
            <h1 id="front-h">Email validation and tracked delivery</h1>
            <p>This server runs catto-mail. The client applications of this installation check addresses and send their email through it, and it
                handles bounces, complaints and suppressions for them.</p>
            <p class="front-actions">{% if public_sign_up_open() %}<a class="btn" href="{{ path('dashboard_sign_up') }}">Sign up</a>{% endif %}<a class="btn{{ public_sign_up_open() ? ' btn-secondary' : '' }}" href="{{ path('dashboard_login') }}">Sign in</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ path('docs_api') }}">API documentation</a></p>
        </section>
        <section class="card front-card g-col-4 md:g-col-2 xl:g-col-1" aria-labelledby="front-signin-h">
            <h2 id="front-signin-h">{{ icon.i('access', 22) }}Operators and clients</h2>
            <p>Sign in to the dashboard with your email address: a single-use link arrives by email. There are no passwords.</p>
            {% if public_sign_up_open() %}
            <p>Open an account yourself: give your organisation and your email address, and confirm the link we send. New accounts start with low sending limits.</p>
            <p><a href="{{ path('dashboard_sign_up') }}">Sign up</a> · <a href="{{ path('dashboard_login') }}">Sign in</a></p>
            {% else %}
            <p>There is no public sign-up: accounts are opened by invitation.</p>
            <p><a href="{{ path('dashboard_login') }}">Sign in</a></p>
            {% endif %}
        </section>
        <section class="card front-card g-col-4 md:g-col-2 xl:g-col-1" aria-labelledby="front-api-h">
            <h2 id="front-api-h">{{ icon.i('send', 22) }}Client applications</h2>
            <p>Applications submit validation and send jobs to the <code>/v1</code> API with an API key, and learn the outcome of each message from
                signed webhooks or by asking the API.</p>
            <p><a href="{{ path('docs_api') }}">API documentation</a></p>
        </section>
        <section class="card front-card g-col-4 md:g-col-2 xl:g-col-1" aria-labelledby="front-mail-h">
            <h2 id="front-mail-h">{{ icon.i('inbox', 22) }}Received mail sent through this server?</h2>
            <p>It was sent for the organisation named as its sender, one of this installation's clients. To stop receiving its mail, use the
                unsubscribe link in the message, if it has one, or contact that sender.</p>
            <p>Some messages link to a page here where you can say whether you still want mail from that sender, or ask never to receive mail
                through this service again.</p>
            <p>To report unwanted mail, {% if admin %}email the administrator at <a href="mailto:{{ admin }}">{{ admin }}</a>.{% else %}contact the administrator of this installation.{% endif %}</p>
        </section>
        <section class="card front-card g-col-4 md:g-col-2 xl:g-col-1" aria-labelledby="front-links-h">
            <h2 id="front-links-h">{{ icon.i('link', 22) }}Links in messages</h2>
            <p>When a sender turns tracking on, the links in a message and a small image point to this server. It records that the message was
                opened or a link was clicked, then sends you straight on to the link's address. It sets no cookies.</p>
            <p>Many mail programs load images on their own, so a recorded open does not prove that anyone read the message.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</main>
{{ site.footer() }}
</body>
</html>
